meta {
  name: Trade a refresh token for new tokens
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~expiresIn: 
  ~refreshExpiresIn: 
  ~delay: 
  ~status: 
  ~fail: 
}

body:json {
  {
    "refreshToken": "suppellex a"
  }
}

docs {
  Answers a new pair, read again from the user's current record. Tokens are not stored, so an old refresh token keeps working until it expires.

  **Not security.** Every account takes the password `password`, and tokens are HS256 JWTs signed with the published key `rest-in-pieces-not-a-secret`, so anyone can mint one. They exist so a frontend can rehearse a sign-in form, protected routes, roles and expired tokens against realistic answers.
}
